1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,380
This is the implementation demo for journey ten.

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:07,540
It is the real application and API running on this machine,

3
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:12,050
with synthetic people and Chromium's fake camera and microphone.

4
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:14,650
Nothing is recorded, charged or sent.

5
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:19,660
It shows a buyer and a mechanic joining the same live video inspection.

6
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:24,600
On the left is the buyer, and on the right is the mechanic,

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,780
each in their own browser session.

8
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:30,890
The buyer opens the booked inspection and chooses Join the call.

9
00:00:30,890 --> 00:00:35,130
The lobby checks the camera and microphone, and lists who is here.

10
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:38,210
The mechanic and the seller have not joined yet.

11
00:00:38,210 --> 00:00:41,300
The buyer joins, and the mechanic does the same.

12
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:46,240
Now each sees the other's live video, and the buyer is told that the mechanic

13
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:46,690
joined.

14
00:00:46,690 --> 00:00:49,900
The video flows directly between the two browsers.

15
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,960
The server only introduces them.

16
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:55,180
The mechanic runs the checklist.

17
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:58,230
Marking brakes done moves the call on to tires,

18
00:00:58,230 --> 00:01:00,630
and the buyer's list changes at once.

19
00:01:00,630 --> 00:01:04,190
The mechanic adds a note, and it appears for the buyer.

20
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:06,780
Only the mechanic has these two buttons.

21
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:10,220
The buyer can watch, but cannot change the checklist.

22
00:01:11,370 --> 00:01:13,510
Now the buyer's connection is cut.

23
00:01:13,510 --> 00:01:16,210
The call says so, and reconnects by itself,

24
00:01:16,210 --> 00:01:19,730
so the buyer keeps their place and the video comes back.

25
00:01:19,730 --> 00:01:22,870
If it could not reconnect after about six seconds,

26
00:01:22,870 --> 00:01:26,390
it would say disconnected and offer one click to rejoin.

27
00:01:26,390 --> 00:01:28,780
To finish, the buyer chooses End call.

28
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:32,180
The dialog asks first, with Stay on the call selected,

29
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:34,310
and says who will be disconnected.

30
00:01:34,310 --> 00:01:35,760
Ending is for everyone.

31
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:40,100
Both sides see the call length, and what was checked and not checked.

32
00:01:41,250 --> 00:01:45,170
The rules are enforced by the server, not just the screens.

33
00:01:45,170 --> 00:01:48,620
A buyer who is not on the inspection gets not found,

34
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,750
so nothing about it is revealed.

35
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:53,540
With no token, the answer is unauthorized.

36
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:58,130
The buyer who booked it cannot run the checklist, and gets forbidden,

37
00:01:58,130 --> 00:01:59,660
while the mechanic can.

38
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:03,980
Ending the call twice gives the same answer, and changes nothing.

39
00:02:05,130 --> 00:02:06,870
Here is what to remember.

40
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:10,150
Two real sessions share one call, peer to peer.

41
00:02:10,150 --> 00:02:13,280
Only the people on the inspection can see it,

42
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:16,140
and only the mechanic runs the checklist.

43
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:21,720
A dropped connection recovers by itself, and ending a call ends it for everyone.

44
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:26,040
Not built yet: recording, the seller joining from a text link,

45
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:28,410
and calls across strict firewalls.

46
00:02:28,410 --> 00:02:32,870
Next, journey eleven: receive the safety certification estimate.
